  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.048,
            0.419,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.089,
            0.539,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two methods of solving this are shown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.119,
            0.476,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "With respect to the buying price being 100%, the selling price is 18% less than the buying price. That is, the selling price would be 82%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.211,
            0.481,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "82% of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2650 = 0.82 \\times 2650 = 2173."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.502,
            0.119,
            0.813,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The loss amount is 18% of 2650. That is, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{18}{100} \\times 2650 = 477."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Reducing this from the buying price, 2650 – 477 = 2173."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.241,
            0.681,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sale amount of the damaged vase would be ₹2173."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.271,
            0.705,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Due to heavy rains, Snehal could not transport strawberries to Hyderabad from his farm in Panchgani. He sells some of his stock at ₹80 per kg with a 12% loss. What is the cost price?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.351,
            0.705,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have probably seen percentages mentioned when shops offer discounts! Do you know what 30% off (or 30% discount) means? It means that the shop is willing to reduce the price of the item by 30%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.721,
            0.25,
            0.932,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.721,
                0.25,
                0.932,
                0.468
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_17_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.435,
            0.719,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ A utensil store is offering a 35% discount on the cooker with an MRP ₹1800. What is the selling price? If the cost"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.473,
            0.789,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "price was ₹900, what is the percentage profit made after the sale?"
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.514,
            0.831,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose Kishanlal achieved a sales of ₹80,000 last month. Out of this, the amount he spent on buying these goods he sold last month was ₹48,000. The difference amount, ₹80,000 – ₹48,000 = ₹32,000, is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "gross profit.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.588,
            0.831,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After deducting the other expenses he incurred (such as transport cost, employee’s salary, electricity bill, etc.) amounting to ₹8,000, the amount remaining is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "net profit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", which is ₹32,000 – ₹8,000 = ₹24,000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.665,
            0.729,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note: In this chapter, the term profit refers to gross profit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.71,
            0.597,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Manisha sells fertiliser. She buys 50 kg bags at ₹500 per bag. She sells it at ₹750 per bag making a profit of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{250}{500} \\times 100 = 50\\%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.773,
            0.597,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Although, with respect to the ₹750 amount she has earned by selling a bag, the profit percentage is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{250}{750} \\times 100 = 33.33\\%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.835,
            0.598,
            0.928
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Profit percentage is calculated based on the price the goods bought when we want to know “How much profit did I make compared to what I invested in buying the goods?”."
            }
          ]
        },
